    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Sr-Lecturer--CET---SkillsFuture----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000042949-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer (CET & SkillsFuture) - School of Business Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Lecturer will be responsible for promoting and expanding adult training courses, developing and executing marketing and outreach initiatives, leading digitalisation and process improvement initiatives and ensuring the successful delivery of the training programmes. This role involves operations, administration, business development, digitalisation and process improvement and teaching to support adult education training. The successful candidate will be an effective communicator, capable of engaging with adult learners and leveraging marketing strategies to enhance course visibility and demand. [What you will be working on] Engage industry partners to offer industry-relevant CET programmes to meet their learning needs and drive enrolment growth. Develop and execute marketing and outreach initiatives for CET programmes to drive programme awareness and learner recruitment. Manage the end-to-end administration of CET programmes and short courses in areas of planning, scheduling, admissions, setup, orientation, student progression, and feedback management. Lead and support digitalisation / automation / process improvement initiatives. Responsible for learning unit development, delivery, internship / project supervision, assessment setting and marking for both full time and part time courses. Mentor and guide learners in their holistic development. Contribute to school-wide events and activities. Undertake any other duties as assigned that support school's vision. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Business-related or IT discipline. Proven experience in business development, marketing, data analysis or process automation. Proficient in digital marketing tools (social media platforms, Google Ads, email marketing tools, etc.). Proficient in Microsoft Power BI / Power Automate. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Meticulous and results-orientated. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks, prioritise workload to meet deadlines and adapt effectively to changes / requirements"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Sr-Lecturer--Supply-Chain---Logistics-Mgt----Sch-of-Business-Mgt_JR-10000051056": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Supply Chain & Logistics Management) - Sch of Business Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Business Management is seeking a Lecturer in Supply Chain & Logistics Management. This position is responsible for developing and delivering comprehensive Diploma and Specialist Diploma programmes, focusing on areas such as supply chain operations with technology and AI applications, sustainability and data analytics. The Lecturer will also actively manage and coordinate learners’ activities and industry-based projects. [What you will be working on] Plan, develop, and deliver learning units within the Supply Chain and Logistics curriculum with technology and AI applications, including conducting assessments, maintaining academic standards, and adopting innovative pedagogical methods. Review and update course content to maintain alignment with current supply chain industry trends, technologies, AI applications and best practices. Organise and lead company visits for the learners to acquire industry best practices. Plan and conduct immersive overseas learning journeys to cultivate global competencies and expose learners to international business, supply chain operations & technologies. Partner with industry partners to solicit feedback on learning unit content and outcomes to create a jointly developed curriculum that maximises learning. Cultivate partnerships with industry stakeholders to collaborate on training initiatives, curriculum development, and professional networking events that benefit learners and the institution. Provide guidance on academic performance, career planning, and overall well-being for the learners throughout their diploma journey. Perform administrative duties related to academic matters, departmental operations, and general administrative support. Support any section projects and ad-hoc assignments when needed. [What we are looking for] Candidates should have three or more years of experience across various supply chain domains, as well as experience using relevant supply chain technology and AI applications. Candidates with a foundation in supply chain management who can deliver learning units in Statistics and/or Economics can also apply. Able to deliver engaging lessons in various supply chain areas such as technology and generative AI applications in supply chain management, inventory and warehouse management, supply chain analytics, sustainability in supply chain, international freight and trade management. Skilful in leading and guiding learners through hands-on activities and projects. Strong, established networks and relationships within the relevant industry or related sectors. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective working relationships across all organisational levels. Possess sound planning, organising and multi-tasking skills, with a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned duties on time."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Banking---Finance----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000047563": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Banking & Finance) - School of Business Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join a team of dynamic professionals at the School of Business Management, where you will play a pivotal role in shaping the future leaders of the Banking and Finance industry. As a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, you will not just be imparting knowledge; you will be nurturing untapped potential, fostering a culture of innovation and ethical responsibility in areas like Sustainable Finance, Digital Banking, and AI in Finance. You will mentor and coach students not only in academic pursuits but also in their holistic development, preparing them to make impactful contributions to society. Your cross-departmental projects and collaborations with industry partners will keep our curriculum at the cutting edge, ensuring our students are equipped for the challenges and opportunities of the rapidly evolving financial landscape. This is more than a teaching role; it is an opportunity to make a lasting difference in the lives of your students and, by extension, the industry at large. [What you will be working on] Responsible for module development, delivery, project supervision, assessment setting and marking for full-time and part-time courses. Coach and mentor both PET and CET learners and be involved in student development activities beyond the classroom. Support and guide learners in their holistic development, including providing pastoral care, supervision for projects and competitions. Mentor learners during Internship Programme. Lead cross-departmental projects that impact the institution. Develop strong relationships and collaborate on projects with industry partners as well as plan, coordinate and execute events for alumni. Participate in the delivery of outreach activities to market the school and course to potential students. Perform administrative and academic duties. [What we are looking for] Candidates who can effectively facilitate not just learning but also the development of practical competencies in learners will have a distinct advantage. Candidates must possess a genuine passion for fostering growth and developing the untapped potential in each learner. Relevant qualification in Banking and/or Finance. At least 3 year(s) of relevant experience in two or more of the following areas for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET): Risk and Compliance Management Fund Management and Administration Consumer and/or Corporate Banking Sustainable Finance AI and Data Analytics in Finance Digital Banking and FinTech Blockchain and Decentralised Finance Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills are essential, along with the capacity to work well in a team, manage deadlines effectively, and handle multiple tasks simultaneously. Proficient in managing administrative tasks with meticulous attention to detail and accuracy. IT savvy with proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite for general tasks, Tableau for data visualization, Python for data analysis or machine learning, and familiar with educational software like Panopto and various Learning Management Systems for effective teaching and learning."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Cybersecurity----School-of-Engineering_JR-10000045420": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Cybersecurity) – School of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This is a full-time Lecturer position dedicated to delivering high-quality education in the field of cybersecurity. The role involves teaching and mentoring learners across foundational cybersecurity concepts, alongside broad-based exposure to cloud computing and software fundamentals. The successful candidate will contribute to curriculum delivery, provide academic guidance, and help learners build essential skills for technology careers. The role will also support industry-relevant student projects and collaborate with internal and external partners. [What you will be working on] The successful candidate will: Facilitate learning units covering fundamental cybersecurity concepts (threats, risk management, and basic security technologies), network security, cloud computing principles, and foundational software systems. Supervise student projects and provide academic guidance.  Develop and update training materials and student assessments.  Support curriculum reviews and academic operations. Stay current with emerging technology trends, integrate updated practices into teaching, and support industry-aligned learning initiatives. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] We are seeking a candidate who possesses: Degree in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a closely related discipline. Solid grounding in cybersecurity fundamentals, coupled with broad-based knowledge in cloud computing architecture and services, and basic software development principles. Experience or familiarity with standard security tools, cloud platforms (such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud), and common software environments. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a clear interest in teaching, guiding, and supporting learners.  Certifications (Advantage): Certifications such as CompTIA Security+, Network+, AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner, Microsoft Certified: Azure Fundamentals, or CEH."
    },
