    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP/Senior--Lead-Executive--HR-Operations_JR-10000054213": {
      "title": "Senior/ Lead Executive, HR Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will play a key role in delivering efficient, compliant, and service-oriented HR operations in support of the organisation’s workforce needs. The role involves overseeing HR processes, advising stakeholders on HR policies and procedures, strengthening data and governance practices, and driving continuous improvements to enhance operational effectiveness and employee experience. [What you will be working on] Specifically, the roles would include but not limited to: Oversee and ensure the effective delivery of end-to-end employee lifecycle processes for Adjunct Lecturers and temporary staff, including appointment administration, onboarding, contract renewals, cessation, records management, and offboarding,with a strong emphasis on governance, accuracy and service excellence. Support stakeholders on HR policies, procedures and best practices, ensuring alignment with organisational guidelines and regulatory requirements. Monitor and review HR operational processes to ensure consistency, compliance and continuous improvement. Work closely with HR Business Partners and internal stakeholders to support workforce planning, employee matters and the implementation of HR initiatives at the operational level. Submit workmen compensation reports to the Ministry of Manpower and ensure timely follow-up on workplace injury compensation matters. Lead or support initiatives to streamline and automate HR processes, leveraging digital tools to improve operational efficiency and enhance service delivery. [What we are looking for] Tertiary qualification in Business, Human Resources, or a related discipline. Minimum 3–5 years of relevant HR experience, with exposure to handling HR operations Good understanding of local labour laws and HR governance practices. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with proficiency in Microsoft Excel. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage stakeholders. Hands-on experience with Workday is advantageous."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive--CET----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000054149": {
      "title": "Executive CET School of Business Management JR 10000054149",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content Sign In Search For Jobs On Careers@Gov The page you are looking for doesn't exist. © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Adjunct-Lecturer---Parademic_JR-10000050883": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer - Paramedicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] This adjunct position offers an opportunity for practicing professionals to educate and mentor the next generation of paramedics on a flexible, part-time basis. As a subject matter expert, you will be responsible for delivering theoretical knowledge and practical skills across various diploma levels, ensuring the curriculum remains grounded in current industry standards. Beyond classroom instruction, this role focuses on shaping the professional character of students through targeted mentorship and the modelling of ethical conduct. [What you will be working on] Deliver lectures, conduct tutorials, and facilitate discussions for pre-hospital emergency care modules at diploma and advanced diploma levels. Impart theoretical knowledge with an emphasis on practical applications in both civilian and/or military contexts. Conduct practical evaluations, and assessments to measure learners’ proficiency and understanding of paramedic concepts. Stay updated on the latest developments in emergency medical services and incorporate current practices and technologies into the program. Instil values of professionalism, compassion, and ethical conduct in learners. Work alongside colleagues, industry professionals, and healthcare organizations to improve the relevance of the educational experience. Maintain a commitment to personal and professional development regarding medical practices and teaching methodologies. [What we are looking for] Relevant Paramedicine qualifications. Qualifications from overseas paramedic programs will also be considered. A minimum of 5 years of experience in emergency ambulance services in Singapore, with a demonstrated understanding of real-world scenarios. Strong verbal and written communication abilities to effectively convey complex concepts and facilitate learning. Strong skills in building positive, collaborative relationships with students, colleagues, and industry professionals. An effective planner capable of sequencing learning to successfully build student knowledge and skills. The ability to serve as a role model through a high level of professionalism in appearance, conduct, and communication."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer---Senior-Lecturer--Medical-Sciences----School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000035150": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Snr Lecturer (Medical Sciences) - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] [What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach Medical Science modules such as anatomy, physiology, pharmacology and pathophysiology for Nursing, Paramedic and Oral Health Therapy learners at Diploma, Specialist Diploma and Advanced Diploma levels. [What you will be working on] Conduct lectures, tutorials, lab sessions, project supervision for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners. Plan and develop course curricula. Perform mentoring duties to assigned group of learners. Participate in committees/workgroups within NYP or with external stakeholders as assigned. Lead/co-lead overseas educational and learning programmes, immersion trips or events etc. to develop students as global citizens. [What we are looking for] At least 3 years of relevant working experience in the Singapore hospital setting as a medical officer. MBBS or equivalent qualification & recency in local clinical practice. Candidate must have current/valid SMC Registration. Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individuals who possess strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills. Good at thinking from a human-centric perspective; working in cross-functional teams; strength in resourcing, critical thinking, sense making; taking initiative; being tenacious and persevering in ambiguous complex situations; able to organize and manage multiple tasks concurrently."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Nursing----School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000034905": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Nursing) - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-12-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach Nursing modules for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET). [What you will be working on] Conduct lectures, tutorials, lab sessions, project supervision for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners. Plan and develop course curricula . Supervise and assess learners in the clinical areas . Perform mentoring duties to assigned group of learners. Participate in committees/workgroups within NYP or with external stakeholders as assigned. Lead/co-lead overseas educational and learning programmes, immersion trips or events etc. to develop students as global citizens. [What we are looking for] At least 5 yrs of clinical experience with at least 2 yrs in one of the specialty areas listed . Relevant qualification in Nursing & recency in local clinical practice . Candidate must have current/valid Singapore Nursing Board (SNB) practising certificate . Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individual who possesses strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills. Good at thinking from a human-centric perspective; working in cross-functional teams; strength in resourcing, critical thinking, sense making; taking initiative; being tenacious and persevering in ambiguous complex situations; able to organize and manage multiple tasks concurrently. ​ Candidate should possess relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: Chronic Disease Management Clinical Education Critical Care Diabetes Management & Education Endoscopy Gerontology Medical-Surgical Nephro-Urology Neuroscience Oncology Orthopaedics Paediatrics Palliative Care Perioperative Perianesthesia Radiology Simulation Based Learning"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Short-Term-Clinical-Instructor---School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000005027-1": {
      "title": "Short Term Clinical Instructor - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] [What the role is] We are looking for individuals to join the School of Health & Social Sciences as Short-Term Clinical Instructors. In this role, you will serve as a role model and mentor for our nursing students and is responsible for providing effective instruction, assessment and support to Nursing students during their clinical placement in hospital and community facilities. You should strive to stimulate the student's interest in all aspects of clinical practice and encourage innovative thinking and approaches to practice. [What you will be working on] Orientate students to the clinical sites including working schedule, assessment methods, and overall responsibilities. Ensure that the clinical practicum facilitates the achievement of stipulated clinical learning outcomes and provide regular feedback to the Clinical Placement Provider to improve the quality of students’ clinical experiences. Support faculty with the development and achievement of the objectives and competencies for clinical skills logbook and assessments. Identify and assign appropriate activities align to the objectives and competencies for the clinical placement to enhance student learning. Impart and enhance students’ understanding of clinical related issues. Assess student’s competency to identify strengths and address weaknesses and monitor their progress to ensure stated objectives are met. Facilitate and seek interactions with the management and other health care professionals of clinical practice sites and act as point of contact for the respective hospitals. Communicate with the clinical manager with any concerns or questions regarding student progress as soon as issues arise. Prepares the staff weekly roster and submit weekly reports to the clinical manager. Maintain student confidentiality and any other duties as assigned [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in nursing At least 3 years clinical experience in acute health care settings Current knowledge of Nursing skills, trends and issues Holds a valid RN license with Singapore Nursing Board Good grasp of computer literacy and demonstrated ability to integrate technology into the learning environment and teaching methodology Good verbal and written communication skills and a demonstrated competency to interact with people at all levels of the organization Effective presentation and demonstration skills, both theoretical and practical Strong interpersonal skills, innovative, team player Able to multi-task Evidence of a personal & professional development plan Teaching experience or qualification will be an advantage"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP/Secretary--Senior-Management-Office-_JR-10000055499": {
      "title": "Secretary (Senior Management Office)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Provide high-level administrative and secretarial support to the senior management team, ensuring smooth operations and coordination of governance-related activities. [What you will be working on] Executive Support Personal Assistant to Chairman (BOG) and two Senior Directors. Manage calendars, schedule meetings, and coordinate appointments. Handle first level enquiries from public, colleagues, students and parents. Handle confidential correspondence and documentation. Office Management Oversee the Chairman’s office space, ensuring cleanliness and operational readiness of equipment and facilities. Jointly manage Huddle’s office space with other Secretaries, including asset management and budgets. Works as a team with other Secretaries and cover each other’s duties when required. Events & Administrative Support Assist in organizing BOG-related events (e.g. lunches & visits). Support claims and asset-related matters for Chairman and Senior Directors. Maintain accurate records and ensure compliance with organizational policies. [What we are looking for] Prior experience in secretarial or administrative support roles is preferred. Strong organizational, time-management skills and stakeholder management skills. High level of discretion and ability to handle confidential information. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and scheduling tools."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Sr-Lecturer--Accountancy---Finance----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000050354": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Sr Lecturer (Accountancy & Finance) - School of Business Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We're looking for accounting professionals who are genuinely curious about where the profession is heading - not necessarily experts in AI or blockchain, but people who recognise these technologies matter and want to understand why. You'll join a team exploring what accounting education looks like when automation handles the bookkeeping, AI flags anomalies, and blockchain creates immutable audit trails. Your role isn't to have all the answers - it's to help students develop the accounting judgment that matters more when technology handles the technical execution. If you've found yourself wondering which accounting tasks will still require human expertise in five years, or if you've started experimenting with AI tools in your own practice and discovered both their potential and their limitations, you already have the mindset we're building on. [What you will be working on] Teaching accounting fundamentals with an eye toward their application in technology-enabled environments. You'll help students understand why accounting principles matter, not just how to apply them manually—because manual application increasingly isn't what employers need. Designing learning experiences where students use emerging technologies (AI, data analytics tools, automation platforms) as part of their accounting work, discovering through practice when these tools help and when human judgment remains essential. Supervising student projects that explore technology applications in accounting contexts. You'll guide students through ambiguous problems where the answer isn't in a textbook—projects that require both accounting knowledge and willingness to experiment with unfamiliar tools. Collaborating with industry partners on initiatives that explore digital transformation in accounting practice. This is learning alongside students and colleagues, not lecturing from established expertise. Coaching diverse learners across Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes - from school leavers building foundations to experienced accountants updating their skills for changing practice environments. Engaging in curriculum development that keeps pace with professional evolution. You'll work with colleagues to determine which traditional content remains essential and where emerging capabilities should reshape what we teach. Contributing to outreach and student development activities that connect classroom learning with professional practice and performing academic and administrative duties as required. [What we are looking for] Accounting Credentials: Relevant qualification in Accountancy with professional certification (or progress toward certification) from recognised accounting bodies such as ISCA, ACCA, CPA Australia, or equivalent. Professional Experience: Substantive work experience in accounting contexts - financial accounting, assurance, internal controls, cost accounting, or related areas. Technology Curiosity: You don't need to be a data scientist or blockchain developer, but you should be genuinely interested in how technology is reshaping accounting work. Perhaps you've: Started experimenting with AI tools for accounting tasks and discovered interesting limitations Wondered which parts of your current role could be automated and which couldn't Found yourself in conversations about RPA, data analytics, or emerging technologies and wanted to understand more Recognised that \"this is how we've always done it\" increasingly isn't sufficient justification Learning Orientation: Comfortable navigating ambiguity and learning alongside students rather than having to be the expert in everything. When faced with unfamiliar technology, your instinct is curiosity rather than resistance. Teaching Capability: Ability to explain complex accounting concepts clearly and make connections between theory and practice. This might be formal teaching experience, training colleagues, or helping others understand accounting implications in business contexts. Digital Comfort: Proficient with digital tools for productivity and communication. If you've explored tools like Power BI, UiPath, or AI platforms, that's valuable—but more important is willingness to engage with new technologies as they emerge. Communication Skills: Ability to work effectively with young adults, adult learners, industry partners, and academic colleagues. You can translate between accounting language and everyday understanding. Collaborative Mindset: Enthusiasm for working with colleagues exploring similar questions about accounting education's future, and with industry partners navigating their own digital transformation journeys."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive-Senior-Executive--Administration----Sch-of-Engineering_JR-10000055349": {
      "title": "Executive/Senior Executive (Administration) - Sch of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a proactive and resourceful professional to support school operations, facilities management, AV systems, project coordination, procurement, security access, and administrative functions. [What you will be working on] Provide operational and technical support for the School's Audio Visual (AV) systems and facilities. Involve in facilities development and improvement projects, including system upgrades, renovations, furniture procurement, and space enhancement initiatives. Manage vendors, contractors, and service providers to resolve facilities-related issues and ensure timely follow-up. Maintain and oversee facilities and asset management records, including finance and procurement documentation, databases, and reporting. Provide logistical and operational support for school events, activities, and programmes. In charge of keys and security management (e.g. card access control) within the school. Coordinate and administer staff seating allocation and workspace arrangements. Work closely across schools and corporate departments on administrative and operational matters. Provide a broad range of administrative support for the departments. Participate in School-wide and Polytechnic-level committees, projects, and initiatives. Support other admin teams (e.g. Assets and Staff Team), when required. Carry out any other ad hoc duties or tasks assigned. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications with a minimum of 3 years of relevant working experience. Experience in facilities, operations, project coordination, or administrative support will be an advantage. Strong organizational, planning, and coordination skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Proactive, meticulous and detail-oriented individual to support the school’s facilities, operations and administrative functions. Positive attitude, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to work collaboratively in a team environment. Self-motivated and resourceful, with the ability to work independently while managing multiple tasks effectively."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Adjunct-Lecturer---Sch-of-Applied-Science_JR-10000054992": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer - Sch of Applied Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] Successful candidates will be involved in the teaching of full time (PET) and/or part time (CET) polytechnic students for various diplomas in the School of Applied Science. [What you will be working on] Successful candidates will develop course materials (where applicable) and facilitate content delivery according to syllabus, be involved in assessment preparation and marking as well as providing teaching-related administrative support. They are also expected to manage digital platforms such as the Learning Management System (LMS), execute interactive digital tools (e.g. Kahoot, Mentimeter) and conduct lessons through face-to-face and/or online modes. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Candidates should possess either one of the following qualifications or its equivalent, with relevant work experience. Biomedical/Life Sciences, Data Science degree or equivalent Chemical Engineering degree or equivalent Food Science degree or equivalent  Health Sciences, Life Sciences, Nursing degree or equivalent Those with experience in one or more of the areas listed below are preferred: Biomedical Science with Analytics At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one of more of the following areas: Clinical Laboratory Sciences (e.g. Clinical Chemistry, Blood Banking, Histopathology, Laboratory Quality Management, Clinical Laboratory Operations) Bioinformatics Database Design & Administration Predictive Analytics & Forecasting Predictive Modelling Biopharmaceutical & Chemical Engineering At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one or more of the following areas: Biologics Upstream Operations Biologics Downstream Operations Manufacturing Science and Technology Food & Beverage Business At least 8 years of relevant work experience in Western cuisine, preferably with supervisory experience in professional kitchens, fine-dining establishments, or modern restaurant operations Demonstrates a strong commitment to keeping abreast of current industry trends and developments, including sustainability practices, evolving dietary needs, and emerging culinary technologies. Demonstrates excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with proven expertise in recipe development and the ability to develop innovative culinary solutions. Pharmaceutical Science At least 3 years of relevant work experience in one or more of the following areas: Nursing / Patient Care Skills (e.g., First Aid, Phlebotomy, ECG monitoring and interpretation, Parenteral Drug Administration) Research Ethics Good Clinical Practice Clinical Trials Management AI & Data Analytics Clinical sample processing For the role related to Pharmaceutical Science, candidates with Singapore Nursing Board (SNB) registration will have an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Paramedicine----School-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000055276": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Paramedicine) - School of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a dedicated individual to join us as a Paramedicine Lecturer. In this role, you'll guide students in pre-hospital emergency care by delivering lectures, practical demonstrations, and facilitating discussions. Using your experience in emergency medical services, you'll provide insights to prepare students for real-world challenges. As part of our team, you'll also contribute to curriculum development, design assessments, and stay updated on industry advancements. This role includes mentoring students during clinical placements and promoting values of professionalism and ethical conduct. If you're passionate about educating the next generation of paramedics, we encourage you to apply for this fulfilling position. [What you will be working on] * Develop and deliver engaging lectures, practical sessions, and clinical simulations in various paramedicine-related modules. * Design, develop, and review curriculum content to ensure alignment with industry standards, regulatory requirements, and pedagogical best practices. * Assess student learning through a variety of methods, provide constructive feedback, and maintain accurate records of student progress. * Mentor and guide students in their academic and professional development, including clinical placements and projects. * Participate in academic administration duties, including course coordination, committee work, and programme review. * Engage in continuous professional development and maintain currency in paramedicine practice and educational methodologies. * Establish and maintain strong industry links to enhance student learning experiences and foster collaboration opportunities. * Contribute to school and poly-wide initiatives and projects. * Supervise student projects, internships, and clinical attachments.   [What we are looking for] Hold a recognized Paramedicine qualification (or equivalent); international paramedic qualifications will be considered. Paramedic Level 4 registration/credential preferred. Minimum of 5 years of active experience in prehospital emergency medical services, with deep practical understanding of real-world clinical scenarios. Proven ability to translate complex clinical concepts into clear, engaging, and effective learning experiences. Strong instructional planning skills, with expertise in sequencing curricula to progressively build student knowledge and practical competency. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills across academic and clinical contexts. Strong interpersonal abilities to build collaborative relationships with students, faculty, and industry partners. High level of professional integrity, serving as a role model in conduct, appearance, and clinical ethics."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Senior-Lead-Executive---Centre-for-Service-Excellence_JR-10000048906": {
      "title": "Senior/Lead Executive - Centre for Service Excellence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As a Senior/Lead Executive of Centre for Service Excellence, you will contribute to the service delivery and experience segment by ensuring our diverse stakeholder groups including current and prospective learners, industry partners and the public are provided with optimal experience in NYP. Your role will encompass implementing effective service solutions involving customer journey mapping to manage both routine and complex cases such as complaints, feedback, and quality service matters. The ideal candidate will balance strategic planning with operational efficiency, demonstrating exceptional written communication and good analytical skill to uphold NYP’s service standards and to foster positive relationships with diverse stakeholder groups. [What you will be working on] Case Management and Service Operations Manage day-to-day operations of customer service & engagement seamlessly between physical (e.g. service centre) and digital touchpoints (e.g. contact centre, live chat) to ensure satisfaction and complete the interaction process. Apply a strategic mindset coupled with resourcefulness and meticulous attention to detail, to conduct comprehensive case analyses. Perform joint case management with internal stakeholders to identify solutions for cases arising from complaints, appeals, or issues to identify systemic problems, and determine strategies to prevent future occurrences. Coordinate replies with inputs given by the internal stakeholders according to NYP and PSD SOPs and service standards. Review draft replies for cases that need to be fronted by QSM’s Office. Capture and maintain accurate records of all customer interactions in the case management system, ensuring data is current and compliant with governance policies. Provide guidance to new and existing team members through on-the-job training/support in case management system and handling of daily operations tasks and assigned admin tasks. Service Design Support & Process Improvement Contribute to mapping customer journeys across various service touchpoints and identifying pain points or inefficiencies in the current service workflow to suggest improvements to streamline the customer experience. Actively contribute insights from case management and customer interactions to enhance service delivery and experience management by the center and to help ensure customer needs are accurately reflected in the design of new services. Co-lead and collaborate with team members to standardise service processes and protocols to ensure consistency in service delivery across multiple channels. Suggest best practices to enhance process efficiency and quality.  Identify patterns in customer enquiries and service performance. Use analytics to support data-driven decision-making in suggesting areas of improvement or resource allocation adjustments. Track key service delivery metrics and conduct basic analysis of service-related data with data analytics tools such as Excel or Power BI. Conduct basic analysis of service-related data and use data to highlight service bottlenecks or areas requiring intervention. [What we are looking for] Qualifications in Business, Communications, Customer Service, or a related field. 3-5 years of experience in service operations, case management and service communication. Strong verbal and written communication skills are highly essential to manage complex, sensitive and quality service manager (QSM) related cases. Prior corporate communication and QSM experience is an advantage. Proficiency in MS Office apps and/or Power BI to contribute to data-driven service process review. Strategic, meticulous, resourceful with good organisational skills with a commitment to contribute to service innovation projects. Prior experience in working on process improvement or service design project would be an added advantage. Possess effective interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate and influence peers to drive service improvements, interact effectively with internal and external stakeholders, and maintain a cheerful personality and innovative mindset to embrace changes and contribute ideas at work. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Exec-Snr-Exec--Student-Life-Academy---AR----Student-Dev---Alumni-Relations_JR-10000055120-1": {
      "title": "Exec/Snr Exec (Student Life Academy & AR) - Student Dev & Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Support the Student Life Academy and Alumni Relations (SLAR) team in delivering student development and alumni engagement initiatives that foster leadership, life skills, community involvement, and lifelong connections with the institution. This role involves managing student clubs and leaders, coordinating programmes and events, supporting stakeholder engagement, and contributing to data-driven improvements in programme effectiveness. The ideal candidate is passionate about youth development, enjoys working with people, and thrives in a dynamic environment. [What you will be working on] Manage and support assigned student clubs and Co-Curricular Activities (CCAs), ensuring effective operations and compliance with institutional policies and governance requirements. Mentor and guide student leaders in planning and implementing activities, projects, events, and leadership initiatives. Plan, coordinate, and execute student development programmes, workshops, leadership training, and engagement activities. Support alumni engagement initiatives, including networking events, outreach programmes, and volunteer opportunities. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders, including students, alumni, industry partners, vendors, and community organisations to deliver meaningful programmes. Manage event logistics, communications, registrations, procurement processes, and administrative requirements to ensure smooth programme execution. Collect, maintain, and analyse programme data, and assist in preparing reports and dashboards to evaluate outcomes and engagement levels. Support departmental projects and initiatives while managing multiple priorities in a dynamic work environment. [What we are looking for] Relevant experience in events, programme coordination, or stakeholder engagement. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage students, stakeholders, and partners effectively. Demonstrated interest in mentoring, youth leadership development, or student engagement activities. Good organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Familiarity with Power BI or data visualisation tools will be an advantage. Resourceful, proactive, and adaptable, with a willingness to learn and grow in a dynamic environment. Passion for student development, leadership cultivation, community engagement, and alumni relations. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Snr-Lead-Exec--Stud-Exp---Digital-Platforms----Stud-Dev---Alumni-Relations_JR-10000054061": {
      "title": "Snr/Lead Exec (Stud Exp & Digital Platforms) - Stud Dev & Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Lead and enhance student experience, engagement, and holistic development initiatives through digital platforms, scholarship programme, and related student engagement programmes and signature events. The role will work closely with stakeholders to design and deliver meaningful student experiences, strengthen student participation, and support students' development journey. In addition, the role will support the administration, enhancement, and optimisation of digital platforms and systems, leveraging technology, data analytics, automation, and user experience improvements to enable effective programme delivery and student engagement. [What you will be working on] Lead and support scholar-related initiatives, including scholarship engagement, development activities, and student recognition programmes. Plan, coordinate, and deliver student engagement programmes, CCA management initiatives, and signature events that foster participation, leadership development, and a vibrant campus experience. Leverage digital platforms and technology-enabled solutions to enhance programme delivery, event management, student engagement, and operational effectiveness. Serve as the product owner for the digital platforms and related student experience systems, driving platform enhancements and continuous improvement. Gather and translate business requirements into digital solutions, system enhancements, automation, dashboards, and workflows that improve student engagement and programme delivery. Collaborate with stakeholders, IT teams, and vendors to implement and maintain digital platforms, integrations, and technologies that strengthen the student experience ecosystem. Manage platform operations, administration, governance, user support, website management, CRM, event systems, and learning platforms to ensure reliable, effective, and user-centric service delivery. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Student Development, Education, Business, Communications, Events Management, Social Sciences, Information Technology, or related disciplines, with the ability to support student engagement, holistic development, scholarship initiatives, CCA activities, and programme delivery. Experience planning, coordinating, and delivering student engagement programmes, leadership development initiatives, scholarship-related activities, CCAs, experiential learning opportunities, or signature events, with a proven ability to create meaningful and impactful student experiences. Strong understanding of student engagement strategies, programme management, stakeholder engagement, and event delivery, with the ability to design and implement initiatives that strengthen student participation, development, and campus life. Experience working with students and diverse stakeholders, including internal departments, external partners, and vendors, to deliver successful programmes, activities, and events that support student growth and engagement. Proficiency in data analytics, reporting tools, Power BI, Excel, and data-driven decision-making, with the ability to monitor participation trends, evaluate programme effectiveness, generate insights, and support continuous improvement. Familiarity with digital platforms, websites, CRM systems, event management platforms, learning management systems, and student-facing applications, with the ability to support platform administration, user adoption, service delivery, and enhancement initiatives. Understanding of business analysis, process improvement, automation, Agile methodologies, design thinking, and user-centred design practices, with the ability to identify opportunities to improve programme delivery and operational effectiveness through technology. Strong stakeholder management, communication, presentation, and project coordination skills, with the ability to engage students, build partnerships, and collaborate effectively across teams to deliver meaningful student experiences and programmes. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a dynamic environment while coordinating scholarship activities, student engagement programmes, CCAs, signature events, and operational responsibilities. Interest in digital innovation, AI, automation, and emerging technologies, with the ability to leverage technology-enabled solutions to enhance student engagement, streamline operations, improve service delivery, and support holistic student development. May be required to plan, organise, and lead students on overseas immersion programmes. Experience in higher education, student development, student affairs, education technology, student systems, engagement platforms, or related environments will be an advantage, particularly in enhancing student participation, development, and overall campus experience. #LI-Onsite"
    },
