    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Precision-Engineering----Sch-of-Engineering_JR-10000055557": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Precision Engineering) - Sch of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join a collaborative team of engineering educators committed to advancing Precision Engineering and smart manufacturing education. You will design and deliver authentic learning experiences in Precision Machining, CAD, Metrology, and Industry 4.0, bridging real-world applications with classroom practice. You will also lead industry collaboration initiatives, mentoring learners to think critically, innovate confidently, and solve complex engineering challenges. You are an industry-engaged practitioner with a passion for emerging manufacturing technologies and a commitment to developing adaptable, future-ready engineering talent. [What you will be working on] Design, develop, and deliver curriculum for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) in areas such as Precision Machining, Computer-Aided Design (CAD), Metrology, and Industry 4.0 technologies. Lead and contribute to the development of applied R&D and industry collaboration projects, especially in CNC machining and Industry 4.0 domains. Guide and mentor learners through academic, project, and career development, including supervision of student projects. Undertake academic-related responsibilities such as lesson planning, assessment, project supervision, and student engagement Support School’s administrative and operational tasks as and when required Keep abreast of and respond to advancements in Precision Engineering landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Relevant degree qualifications in Manufacturing, Mechanical Engineering, or a related field. At least 3 years of relevant industry experience in the Manufacturing or Precision Engineering sector. Candidate should possess relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: CNC Machining (Turning and Milling) Computer-Aided Design and Manufacturing (CAD/CAM) IoT applications in Manufacturing environment Metrology and measurement systems, including use of advanced equipment (e.g., CMM, Vision Systems, 3D Scanners) Proficiency in at least one programming language (e.g., Python, Java, MSSQL) Preferably: Experience in conducting training or delivering technical courses in Precision Engineering topics Experience in sustainability applications in manufacturing Familiarity with AI-based solutions and their implementation within engineering or manufacturing contexts."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-CIL3/Senior-Lead-Exec--Business-Analyst----Centre-for-Industry---Lifelong-Learning_JR-10000050040": {
      "title": "Senior/Lead Exec (Business Analyst) - Centre for Industry & Lifelong Learning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Business Analyst in the OpsTech team will play a crucial role in enhancing operational support and system capabilities for Continuing Education and Training (CET) programs and schools. This role involves analysing business processes, identifying areas for improvement, and implementing solutions to optimise system usage and improve effectiveness and support both ongoing Training Management System operations. [What you will be working on] Nanyang Polytechnic is seeking an experienced and motivated Senior/Lead Executive (Business Analyst) to join our Centre for Industry & Lifelong Learning (CIL3). Job Responsibilities * Provide better support to schools and CET institutes on TMS to optimise system usage and improve effectiveness. * Provide Level 1 support to address user issues, troubleshoot, and coordinate with vendors to resolve system problems * Accelerate change requests and drive enhancements in STEP to better support CET operations and ensure a more responsive system. * Conduct impact analysis on service requests for data patches or change requests. * Assisted in execution of User Acceptance Testing (UAT) plans, coordinating with end-users, and taking charge of issue resolution * Collaborate closely with internal stakeholders (e.g., academic schools, marketing, IT) and external partners (e.g., industry representatives) to understand needs, define requirements, and translate them into practical solutions. * Enhance end-to-end course administration support, including course setup, to streamline processes and improve efficiency. * Work closely with both academic and non-academic staff to ensure smooth management of courses. * Provide general administrative support for the department and maintain proper documentation #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Job Qualifications *Qualifications in Business, Information Systems, or a related field. * Proven years of relevant experience in business analysis, project management, or related field, preferably within the education sector, public sector, or a similar environment focused on lifelong learning. * Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to interpret large datasets and translate them into clear, concise, and actionable insights. * Strong communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders at all levels. * Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced and dynamic environment. * Knowledge of the Singapore education landscape and lifelong learning initiatives will be an advantage."
    },
